The cancelled order says so on the row, not only inside it

Found by driving the DEPLOYED history page against the real sandbox rather
than the test rig: place an order, open it, press plus, press minus, add
something alongside, cancel it, and watch what the screen says.

Everything held except the last one. The row kept saying "With the kitchen"
after the order had been cancelled. The order really was off - the server
said so and meant it - and the screen did not repeat it, which is worse than
not redrawing at all.

The cause is the fix before this one. Redrawing only the details panel
leaves the button above it untouched, and the state badge, the token and the
total all live up there. So the row is rebuilt from the same answer and
dropped in place with its details left OPEN - which is the point of all of
this: the old full repaint rebuilt every row, every panel starts closed, and
the one the customer was looking at shut itself on every single tap. Owner:
"if i click + or - then page restarted and not working." That was not the
limiter, it was this, and it happened every time rather than every fifth.
